nano-mouse: editor-style mouse selection and system clipboard for GNU nano 7.2

  - click and drag to select, with autoscroll at the top and bottom edges
  - double-click selects a word, triple-click a line (drag to extend)
  - Alt+click / Shift+click extends the selection
  - typing, pasting, Backspace or Delete replace a selection
  - every copy and cut also goes to the system clipboard (OSC 52)
  - a one-time hint and a "Mouse actions" section in the ^G help

Applies to the pristine nano-7.2 source (sha256 86f34427...4526):
  cd nano-7.2 && patch -p1 < nano-mouse.patch

https://github.com/DohaerisAI/nano-mouse
License: GPL-3.0-or-later, the same as GNU nano.

